// What each Fabric DATA AGENT costs per question, in CU seconds.
// Run with --capacity <guid> (the runner adds MPARAMETER 'CapacitiesList').
//
// Read the ML row, never the lake rows. One data agent bills under TWO items: a DataAgent
// item (Experience "ML", OperationName "AI Query") carrying the cost of answering the
// question, and an LlmPlugin item (Experience "lake") carrying its OneLake reads and writes.
// Measured on a live F8, the lake side was 0.02% of the total, so reading it instead of the
// ML row understates a question by three orders of magnitude.
//
// This reads Item History rather than 'Metrics By Item And Day' on purpose. The aggregate
// fact tables return NOTHING for an item created the same day, so an agent built this
// morning is invisible there while Item History already has it in full.
//
// Microsoft's published rates: 100 CU s per 1,000 input tokens, 10 per 1,000 cached input
// tokens, 400 per 1,000 output tokens. A capacity's daily budget is SKU x 86,400 CU s
// (F2 = 172,800, F8 = 691,200, F64 = 5,529,600), so CU_s_per_question x expected daily
// questions against that number is the capacity-planning arithmetic.
EVALUATE
ADDCOLUMNS(
    FILTER(
        SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(
            'Item History Main'[WorkspaceName],
            'Item History Main'[ArtifactName],
            'Item History Main'[OperationName],
            'Item History Main'[Experience],
            "CU_s", SUM('Item History Operation'[CU (s)]),
            "Questions", SUM('Item History Operation'[Operations]),
            "Throttling_s", SUM('Item History Operation'[Throttling (s)])
        ),
        [CU_s] > 0
            && 'Item History Main'[OperationName] = "AI Query"
            && 'Item History Main'[Experience] = "ML"
    ),
    "CU_s_per_question", DIVIDE([CU_s], [Questions])
)
ORDER BY [CU_s_per_question] DESC

// --- Both halves of the bill (ML answering + lake file I/O) instead of ML only: drop the
//     Experience predicate and group by it, so the two rows stay separately labelled:
//   FILTER(SUMMARIZECOLUMNS(...), [CU_s] > 0
//       && 'Item History Main'[OperationName] IN {"AI Query", "OneLake Read via Proxy",
//                                                 "OneLake Iterative Read via Proxy"})
